<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 425 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 425 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 425 million stg of unspecified late assistance.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.2 BLN    1.2 BLN    1.05 BLN   1.05 BLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY     50 MLN    209 MLN    527 MLN    952 MLN</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BANK 1 T-BILLS					50 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 1 BILLS			   59 MLN*   228 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BILLS/FRG NOV 15/18   50 MLN#   100 MLN#    40 MLN#   =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED LATE ASSISTANCE				   425 MLN</p>
<p># INTEREST RATE - 5-31/32 PCT</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
